## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Project Name: GovAI Nexus  
Tagline: Smarter Government. Faster Services. Transparent Governance.  
Target: Tamil Nadu Government  
Portal: Employee Portal  
Languages: English + Tamil  
Platforms: Web + Responsive Mobile  
Primary Backend Language: Python  
Frontend: React 19 + Vite + TypeScript  
Backend: Python 3.12+ + FastAPI  
Database: PostgreSQL  
Cache: Redis

You are working on an existing enterprise-level GovTech application called GovAI Nexus.

Your task is to design and implement the complete Employee Portal as an integrated part of the existing GovAI Nexus platform.

The Employee Portal is designed for government employees, e-Sevai operators, junior assistants, clerks, department staff, verification officers and authorized processing personnel.

Its primary responsibility is to help government employees:

- Process citizen applications.
- Verify uploaded documents.
- Manage government service requests.
- Review scheme applications.
- Handle citizen grievances.
- Assign and complete tasks.
- Communicate with citizens.
- Monitor application deadlines.
- Generate departmental reports.
- Improve service delivery efficiency.

IMPORTANT:

1. Follow the existing GovAI Nexus branding and design system.
2. Maintain the same visual consistency as the Citizen Portal.
3. Do not redesign the entire project.
4. Do not remove existing functionality.
5. Do not create a separate disconnected application.
6. Integrate every feature into the existing backend and PostgreSQL database.
7. All dashboard metrics must come from actual database queries.
8. All actions must work through real backend APIs.
9. Do not use hardcoded production data or disconnected mock functionality.
10. Keep advanced department-level administration in the Officer Portal and platform-wide administration in the Super Admin Portal.

